# Line endings.
#
# Git stores text as LF and, with core.autocrlf enabled, rewrites it to CRLF on
# a Windows checkout. For source that is harmless. For anything the Uberspace
# host executes it is fatal: bash stops at the first carriage return with
# "$'\r': command not found", and supervisord reads a trailing \r as part of the
# command path. A clone on Windows would ship a broken installer to the host,
# which is exactly what happened before this file existed.

* text=auto

# Run on the host. These stay LF wherever they are checked out.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.ini text eol=lf

# Never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
